/**
\page org_mitk_editors_report The Report Editor

A report is a document about the data of the session, with text, tables, charts and images of
the display windows. Programs that work with the Workbench through its REST API create reports,
for example the Agent view after a segmentation. Each report opens in an editor of its own, next
to the Standard Display; its tab shows the report's title.

Reports follow the Workbench's theme: a dark page in the dark theme, a light one otherwise. A
report that is saved or opened in the web browser keeps the theme the editor shows, and looks
there as it does in the editor. Printed pages are always light. The editor shows the report but
does not let you select or copy its text; open it in the web browser for that.

\section org_mitk_editors_reportSave Saving a report

"Save as HTML..." saves the report as a single HTML file. Its images are part of the file, so
it can be passed on as it is and opened in any web browser. The file contains no scripts, and a
content security policy keeps browsers from loading anything from elsewhere.

"Open in Browser" shows the report in the web browser, for example to print it or to save it as
a PDF. The browser opens a copy in a temporary folder, which the Workbench removes when it
closes.

\section org_mitk_editors_reportLifetime Closing a report

A report exists only as long as its editor. Closing the editor discards the report, and reports
are not restored when the Workbench starts again. Save a report you want to keep before you
close it.

*/
